From 49c12ce7816ba1567f53283af6c3d1c00814f72a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:51:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Managed workers honour a committed model switch through
 owner-scoped receipt operations

The production worker's RuntimeSessionStore had no get_meta/_write_sql, so pending() silently
returned None and every worker rebuild after a switch hit 'Exact pinned route cannot fail over'.
Intent read/consume are now narrow worker.persist operations (route_switch.pending/consume) bound
to the worker's own assigned session and generation by the receipt fence; SessionDB exposes the
same two methods. Consume is compare-and-delete. An auto build honouring an intent resolves on the
switch's committed provider. The model receipt row writer now moves provider/base_url/api_mode/
gateway_runtime and billing to the picked tuple with update_session_model's merge. route_runtime
pre-build lookups run under temporary_resolution so they mint no standing allocation. [daveey]
